  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>R. Ward, bootmaker, is listed at No. 49 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> in 1920.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>Richard Thomas Ward, bootmaker, is on the 1919 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 49 Madeline Street.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>William Roberts is at No. 47 and B. Singer, whiteworker, at No. 51. In 1905 No. 49 had been the shop of <ref target="civic?id=Carl%20Fischer">Carl Fischer</ref>, hairdresser and tobacconist.</p>
      </div>
